# Notify MRC on MR create or push

> **Captured/Updated**: 2026-08-29
> **Owner**: `@aea-mr-coordinator` with `@aea-project-manager`
> **Traceability**: Issue #315, MR handoff SOP

When anyone opens a GitLab merge request, or pushes a commit that updates an
open MR, **notify `@aea-mr-coordinator`**. Do not wait for the sponsor to say
“MRC proceed”.

## Author (any stakeholder that ships)

After `glab mr create`, or after `git push` to a branch that already has an
open MR:

1. Post a non-resolvable GitLab note on that MR
   (`glab mr note create <n> --resolvable=false`) that MRC has an item to
   gate. Say whether this is a **create** or a **push update**, and the HEAD
   SHA.
2. If this session can continue as MRC, read
   `.cursor/skills/aea-mr-coordinator/SKILL.md` and `gates.md`, then run
   gates. If it cannot, stop after the note — the note is the handoff.
3. Do **not** merge. Do **not** set auto-merge. Only MRC does that.

Do not open a second note on every later push if an unresolved MRC handoff
thread already exists; reply on that thread with the new SHA.

## MRC

A create/push note, or an in-session author handoff after `glab mr create` /
`git push` to an MR branch, **counts as invocation** for that MR. Run gates.
After they pass, set `glab mr merge <n> --yes --auto-merge`. Do not wait for
a second named-MR merge prompt.

Loop ticks still must not merge unless this handoff or an explicit MRC
invocation happened.
